A '''character''' is a player-controlled persona in the game with a unique name in the game world.

==Character creation==
After logging into [[Path of Exile]] a character can be created through the character creation screen.

A character can be created in different [[leagues]] and with additional difficulty options. The game recommends starting in the current challenge league for the most active economy.

Once the league has been chosen, a [[character class]] can be selected. The classes differ by starting location on the [[passive skill tree]], the [[quest rewards]] they're given, by their base [[attributes]] and their general appearance and voice. They also each have different possible [[Ascendancy class]]es.

Players can freely choose their character's name; however, it cannot be assigned to any currently existing characters, and it is not possible to use non-ascii letters or numbers in the name. The only special character allowed is the underscore. If an account has remained inactive for over a year their character names will become available for other players to use when creating a new character.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3418466#p25076686</ref> Names of your existing characters can be changed from the official website [https://www.pathofexile.com/my-account/character-rename here]; players can store up to 20 uses and accumulate two additional uses each week.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/post-reply/3452304/quote/25160731</ref>

By default only 24 characters can be created. After that existing characters have to be deleted in order to create new a one; however this limit can be extended by purchasing additional character slots from the Path of Exile Shop. Up to 255 characters can be created by purchasing [[Extra Character Slot]]s.<ref>https://reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/wquunv/i_just_found_out_you_can_only_have_255_character/
</ref>

==Shared Stats==
The stats found in the subsections can be found on every character, regardless of the [[character class]].
<!-- This data can be found in content.ggpk:Metadata/Characters/Character.ot - update as needed, it is referenced in multiple places -->

===Base Stats===
{{#cargo_query:
|tables = generic_stats
|fields = stat_text
|where = name="Character"
 AND (id="base_evasion_rating" 
 OR  id="base_critical_strike_multiplier" 
 OR  id="energy_shield_recharge_rate_per_minute_%" 
 OR  id="mana_regeneration_rate_per_minute_%")
|format = ul
}}

===Dual Wield===
* 10% more [[Attack Speed]]
* +20% Chance to [[Block]] Attack Damage

===Charges===
{{#cargo_query:
|tables = generic_stats
|fields = stat_text
|where = name="Character"
 AND (id LIKE "%frenzy%charge%"
 OR id LIKE "%endurance%charge%"
 OR id LIKE "%power%charge%"
)
|format = ul
}}

===Maximums===
{{#cargo_query:
|tables = generic_stats
|fields = stat_text
|where = name="Character"
 AND ((
       id LIKE "%max%"
    OR id LIKE "base_number%"
 )
 AND id NOT LIKE "%charge%"
 OR id LIKE "%maximum%rampage%")
|format = ul
}}

===PvP===
{{#cargo_query:
|tables = generic_stats
|fields = stat_text
|where = name="Character" AND id LIKE "%pvp%"
|format = ul
}}

==Character level==
The character level is used for a variety of purposes, most importantly character level will be a limiting factor for [[equipment]]. 

:Note that on specifically [[weapon]] and [[armour (equipment)|armour]] equipment, the base type's level requirement is hidden and ignored for items with a requirement of 4 and lower, as long as their [[modifier]]s do not add a level requirement. For example, {{il|Fishscale Gauntlets}} can be equipped by a Level 1 Character despite the base type having a datamined value of {{c|stat|Requires Level}} {{c|white|4}}; it cannot be equipped if it has {{c|stat|Requires Level}} {{c|white|2}} from the modifier {{ml|LocalIncreasedArmourAndEvasion1}}. A {{il|Short Bow}} cannot be equipped until Level 5, and non-weapon/armour items like {{il|Quicksilver Flask}} still have normal level requirements.

The character level can be increased though gaining [[experience]] which is obtained by killing [[monsters]]. Some encounters may grant deferred experience instead of granting it immediately, such as interrogating [[Immortal Syndicate]] members, or after completing a [[Delve]] encounter.

Once a certain threshold is reached, the character will level up gaining one [[passive skill]] point and granting the following bonuses:

{{#cargo_query:
|tables = generic_stats
|fields = stat_text
|where = name="Character" AND (id LIKE "%per_level%" AND value > 0)
|format = ul
}}

